At Sunrock, we don’t just offer jobs, we offer missions. Are you ready to advance your career and contribute to a sustainable future? As part of our fast‑growing team in Germany, you’ll play a key role in accelerating the clean energy transition across Europe.
 We believe in purpose over routine, people over hierarchy, and progress over comfort zones. Sunrock is a market leader in large‑scale rooftop solar installations in the Netherlands, Germany, and France. But our ambitions go far beyond solar: we deliver integrated energy solutions, including energy management systems, advanced battery storage, and our own energy trading platform.
 In Germany, we’ve already secured over 300 MWp in project volume, focusing on commercial and logistics real estate. As we expand rapidly, we’re strengthening partnerships with key industry players and we’re looking for passionate professionals to join us on this journey. 
 About the role 
 As Technical Project Manager , your mission is to support developing technically feasible projects and to act as a bridge between Technical Experts and Project Development to ensure that all Sunrock projects in development meet the highest technical standards. You will be reporting directly to the Technical Lead Development, and working closely with a team of technical experts and project developers. You have a key role in standardizing technical processes and organizing EPC-tenders to prepare technically sound and cost-optimized projects for execution. 
 Your responsibilities 
 Support developing solar and smart energy projects from proposal phase to financial close, ensuring smooth handover to construction and commissioning; 
 Work closely with other Technical Project Managers to ensure technical feasibility, optimized system design, and compliance with internal standards and regulations; 
 Collect all information and create Request for Quotations (RfQ) for our energy projects in alignment with Technical Team and Project Developers. Detect possible source of error in RfQs to increase the efficiency of EPC Tenders; 
 Act as Technical Gate Keeper by reviewing planning, structural constraints (in collaboration with an external structural engineer) and site visit documentation; 
 Organize with Technical Lead EPC Tenders and support concluding EPC contracts in close collaboration with other internal stakeholders, ensuring alignment on technical scope, risk allocation, commercial terms and timelines; 
 Ensure a smooth transfer to Implementation Team by collecting all the relevant documents and coordinating with other shareholders; 
 Provide technical guidance to Project Developers throughout the development lifecycle and act as technical expert wherever needed i.e. site visits, gathering information etc.; 
 Support the Business Development team with technical assessments of projects or portfolios to ensure high‑quality project origination. 
 What you bring to the table 
 Degree in Engineering, Renewable Energy, Electrical Engineering, or a related technical field; 
 Experience in project development or project management of PV systems; 
 Understanding of PV system design, grid connection requirements, and relevant technical standards; 
 Experience in defining project requirements, evaluating EPC offers, and negotiating technical and commercial terms; 
 Structured, proactive and hands‑on mindset with a high sense of ownership; 
 Fluent in German and English; 
 Willingness to travel as required; based in or near Düsseldorf (or willing to relocate). 
