ERP Application Specialist (NetSuite)   
 at Sunrock B.V.    
 Amsterdam  
 Help us build a future powered by clean energy 
 We’re hiring an ERP Application Specialist in Amsterdam
 Sunrock isn't just another company; we're a vision in action. With a young spirit and a wealth of experience, we're committed to excellence in our quest for sustainable energy solutions. Our growth is rapid and our ambitions are sky high! We cover projects from solar systems to BESS (Battery Energy Storage Systems) and EV solutions, that are all steered by our own EMS (Energy Management System). As Europe's leading name in large-scale solar projects, we're not just part of the industry, we're redefining it. 
 The role   
 As our ERP Application Specialist, you are responsible for the day-to-day management, support and continuous improvement of Sunrock’s NetSuite platform. You ensure the system remains reliable, user-friendly and aligned with business needs across Finance, Asset Management and our commercial team s . Acting as the bridge between users, business stakeholders and external partners, you drive adoption, optimize processes and help maximize the value of the platform. An overview of your responsibilities 
 Act as the primary point of contact for NetSuite users across Sunrock; 
 Provide functional support and resolve application-related issues; 
 Manage users, roles, permissions and system configurations; 
 Configure and maintain workflows, dashboards, forms and integrations; 
 Coordinate testing and validation of system changes and releases; 
 Monitor platform performance, releases and new functionality; 
 Support data quality initiatives and master data management; 
 Identify and implement process improvements that increase efficiency and user adoption; 
 Translate business requirements into practical NetSuite solutions; 
 Train users, coordinate external partners and advise stakeholders on platform capabilities and best practices. 
 What you bring to the table:   
 3-5 years of experience as an ERP Administrator, Application Administrator, or similar role.; 
 Minimum 2 years of hands-on NetSuite experience; 
 Experience with user management, system configuration, application support, and release management; 
 Pro-active mindset, great communication skills and independence; 
 Understanding of ERP processes within Finance and operational environments.; 
 Experience with SuiteScript, SuiteFlow, or NetSuite integrations; 
 Knowledge of Finance and Asset Management processes in the Energy Sector (plus) 
 Experience in a multi-country environment (plus) 
 Familiarity with IT service management and change management processes (plus) 
 What’s in it for you?   
 At Sunrock, work is not just about making a difference in the world - it's also about having fun and enjoying your job. Join our team and benefit from: 
 💰 Salary package of EUR 60.000,- EUR 70.000,- including holiday allowance 
 💰 Annual bonus of up to 11.5% of your salary 
